# Three-agent workflow

For every implementation, the **parent** (this chat) runs this loop. Do not skip a role.

1. **`ux`** — direction or spec first (or confirm there is no visual/copy change). Does not write production code.
2. **`developer`** — implements against that spec. Does not start UX or code review.
3. **`ux`** — PASS/FAIL on the running UI when anything user-visible changed (use screenshots / the browser).
4. **`reviewer`** — PASS/FAIL on the real git diff (`.cursor/rules/code-quality.mdc`). Does not implement.

Loop steps 2–4 until **both** UX and reviewer pass. Then present findings and wait for Gabriel. The reviewer is not a merge gate.

Do not commit or push unless Gabriel explicitly asks.
